//! Repro: comptime-Type-param helper left unspecialized (imm_map family).
//!
//! `Map.insert`'s spec body calls `_node_insert(K, V, root, shift, hash,
//! k, v)` — a module-level helper with `comptime(K/V) : Type` params and
//! SomeT runtime params, NO foralls, NO closure param. The inline-FuncVal
//! arm's codegen-specialization gate required a CLOSURE param (a
//! narrowing TS's isFunctionTypeGeneric guard does not have —
//! helper.ts:1911, guards.ts:457), so the call emitted the BARE generic
//! fid with the Types as runtime C args:
//!   error: call to undeclared function 'yo_id_5430'
//!   yo_id_5430((// Unknown type: Type)(...), ...)
//! Fix (round 2, WIP — scratchpad/round2_param_model_wip.patch): drop the
//! closure-param narrowing + the faithful comptime-param model. BLOCKED on
//! a deeper pattern-era instance leak inside the activated spec bodies —
//! see the "Round-2 outcome" ledger entry
//! (issues/yo-self-gap6-ctor-memo-reconciliation-attempt7.md).
//! Expected when fixed: compiles and runs clean with ZERO
//! "Failed to transpile" markers in the emitted C (TS emits zero).
{ assert } :: import("std/assert");
{ Map } :: import("std/imm/map");
main :: (fn(io : Io) -> unit)({
  m := Map(i32, bool).new();
  m2 := m.insert(i32(3), true);
  assert(m2.len() == usize(1));
  assert(m2.get(i32(3)) == Option(bool).Some(true));
});
export(main);
